Apologies for repeating this. It has been over
six months, so I thought we might have picked up
a few new people.

I am interested in coming up with a diagramming
technique for Lojban comparable to the one that
was drilled into me as a child (for English).
This apparently was the "Reed-Kellogg" technique.

This is NOT because I'm knowledgeable in Lojban.
It's because I'm NOT.

I have found sentence diagramming to be a powerful
analytical tool and learning technique.

Of course, as I learn more, my conception of how
it ought to be done shifts and changes.

At any rate, I am wondering if anyone is interested
in assisting with this project. Reply to me directly
if you wish.

My preliminary efforts are at:
http://hypermetrics.com/lojban/lojdiag.html

However, it's obvious that even at this primitive
stage, it needs some reworking. {nu}, for example,
should be shown as more prominent/important, as
someone said.

I'm currently playing with {bo} and {co}, internal
sumti, and the logical connnectives.


Thanks,
Hal


